2008-01-14  Gavin Salam  <salam@lpthe.jussieu.fr>

        * plugins/SISCone/siscone
	  switched this back over to the SISCone trunk, in preparation for
	  Belyaev's bug fixes.
	
	* regression-tests/2008-01-14-midpoint-jetclu.res: *** ADDED ***
	  results of test to make sure new Midpoint and Jetclu code gives
	  identical jets.

	* plugins/CDFCones/CDFcode/MidPointAlgorithm.cc (MidPointAlgorithm::iterateCone): 
	  modified the procedure that checks if a cone is stable: migrated
	  it from a check on the values of y,phi,pt to a check based on
	  which particles are in/out of the cone. Also replaced a
	  sqrt-based distance comparison with one that looks at the
	  squared distances. 

	  Together with the caching below this gives a quite noticeable
	  speed improvement and eliminates the issue of optimization
	  causing a big slow-down on 32 bit architectures (equality tests
	  on double-prec values for y,phi,pt, in stable-cone check, were
	  comparing 64 bit stored results with 80 bit in-register
	  results).

	* plugins/CDFCones/CDFcode/LorentzVector.hh (class LorentzVector):
	  cached calculation of y, phi to speed up iteration in the
	  midpoint iterations; to do so safely, had to make 4-momentum
	  components private. Added E() method in order to have access to
	  E() needed in JetCluPlugin.

	* plugins/CDFCones/CDFJetCluPlugin.cc: 
	  adapated this to the new form of the CDF LorentzVector.hh class.

